[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3550944410","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112937#issuecomment-3550944410","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112937","id":3550944410,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Tpxya","user":{"login":"darksylinc","id":3395130,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTUxMzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3395130?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc","html_url":"https://github.com/darksylinc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-19T06:02:42Z","updated_at":"2025-11-19T06:03:17Z","body":"This bug is very specific to Polaris cards on Windows drivers.\r\n\r\nIt seems to be very sensitive to submission order, rather than anything else. I suspect any random thing could break it again.\r\n\r\nBut if the results of this workaround works consistently enough, I suggest this fix should only be applied when detecting the affected cards / drivers, rather than applying it unconditionally to all systems, and tag it as a workaround so it can ve properly tracked.\r\n\r\n(That is as long as validation sync isn't failing)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3550944410/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3551720108","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112937#issuecomment-3551720108","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112937","id":3551720108,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7TsvKs","user":{"login":"TacoGuyAT","id":35270005,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MjcwMDA1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35270005?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TacoGuyAT","html_url":"https://github.com/TacoGuyAT","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TacoGuyAT/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TacoGuyAT/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TacoGuyAT/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TacoGuyAT/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TacoGuyAT/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TacoGuyAT/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TacoGuyAT/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TacoGuyAT/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TacoGuyAT/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-19T09:31:12Z","updated_at":"2025-11-19T09:31:12Z","body":"I'm not familiar with Godot's codebase and C++ in general, if there is some existing code I can reference to implement device/driver detection and tailor rendering logic to specific device group - I could implement it myself, but otherwise it would require someone else's help.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3551720108/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_git